PROGRESS 2026-10-21 (third pass) -- a review of the day's own changes found a MAJOR functional bug, and five more.

RENDER() COULD NOT FILL THE RESULT PANE AT ALL. App.tag_links was a @staticmethod whose body read `self._main.tag_links(text, on_click)`, so every call raised NameError: name 'self' is not defined; render() propagated it and the port could not show a translation. Nothing in the suite called render(). Fixed: the delegator forwards the widget (the main window tags its own result pane, the dictionary window its own aux pane) and MainWindow.tag_links is a staticmethod, because the body was a module-level function that took the widget to tag. New tests/regress_delegators.py (54 assertions) walks every Phase 7 delegator: each forwards its arguments, no staticmethod body uses 'self', and render() fills both panes.

Also fixed, from the same review:
* the source pane's fixed height killed the drag-sash and General.MidSplitterPos (the sash set the Text's -height, which no longer decided the visible size) -- the FRAME's height is the pane's now, and it is sized in LINES (native holds ten and a half lines of the help text) so it follows the display's scaling instead of one machine's pixels;
* a restored Contents.EditBackTranslation was invisible: the third pane is packed only while it carries a back-translation and nothing un-packed it after the boot restore;
* pack(before=...) needs a MANAGED reference and the service strip can be hidden -- the TclError was swallowed and the pane never appeared;
* the keyboard's language combo persisted the choice but never re-labelled the keys, and Shift typed Latin capitals on a Cyrillic layout;
* the dictionary's result pane did not fill its frame vertically; the history's new OK button destroyed the window without saving its placement; a _star name collision in the history tree would have stopped the list repainting on a filter change.

The history tree is now native's shape (a single indented column with a star icon and the service's logo, no headings) and the translation is expanded by default, as native's tree always is.

Suite: 132 suites, 0 failed. The row stays UNKNOWN: the human review and the waiver token are still required, and the capture pair needs re-taking because the port has changed since 2026-10-16.
